NSSF statutory contribution, employer's part (10 %) (National Social Security Fund Act Cap. 50 R.E. 2023 s. 12, First Schedule ('Contributions for employees') [text version: Cap. 50 R.E. 2023 (world/B10-anglophone-africa/tz/law/nssf_cap50_re2023.txt)]): First Schedule: statutory contribution for each employee 'Twenty cents for every complete shilling of wages', of which the 'Employer's share deductible from wages by Employer' is 'Ten cents for every complete shilling of wages'; the employer pays the other 10 %.

Skills and Development Levy (3,5 % of gross monthly emoluments) (Vocational Education and Training Act Cap. 82 R.E. 2023 s. 14 (1)-(3) as amended by Act 7 of 2023 s. 73 (TRA PDF, R4/fetch/tz11); Finance Acts 2024 and 2026 amend only s. 19 exemptions): s. 14 (1): levy charged 'from every employer who has in his employment ten or more employees'; (2): 'The levy shall be the sum of money equal to three point five per centum of the total gross monthly emoluments payable by the employer to his employees in respect of that month.' Eighteenth pass: the ten-employee test of s. 14 (1) is applied through kernel 2.6.0 employer facts (Global2.Employer, companies := true): an adult whose employer has fewer than ten employees bears no levy; with no headcount given the employer is presumed in scope, as before. Worked cases (hand): wages 1 000 000, employer of 25 -> 35 000; of 9 -> nothing; of 10 -> 35 000 (inclusive); no headcount -> 35 000 (presumed); company payroll 1 000 000 with 40 employees -> 35 000, with 8 -> nothing.

Workers Compensation Fund contribution, private-sector employer (0,5 %) (Workers Compensation Act Cap. 263; Workers Compensation (Payment of Tariff) Regulations GN 229A of 2017 reg. 5 (2) as amended by GN 496G (1 % -> 0,6 %) and GN 478F of 1 July 2022 (0,6 % -> 0,5 %) (wcf.go.tz PDFs, R4/fetch/tz11) [text version: GN 229A of 2017 as amended by GN 496G and GN 478F of 1 July 2022 (wcf.go.tz PDFs)]): GN 478F reg. 2: 'The principal Regulations are amended in regulation 5 (2) by deleting the words "zero point six per centum (0.6 %)" and substituting for them the words "zero point five per centum (0.5 %)"', in effect from 1 July 2022. -/

namespace TzGlobal
open TaxKernel TaxKernel.Global

def nssf : Family :=
